====Adverb====
{{en-adv|-}}

# {{lb|en|interrogative}} For [[what]] [[cause]], [[reason]], or [[purpose]].
## {{non-gloss definition|Introducing a complete question.}}
##: {{ux|en|'''Why''' is the sky blue?}}
##: {{ux|en|'''Why''' did you do that?}}
##: {{ux|en|I don’t know '''why''' he did that}}
##: {{ux|en|Tell me '''why''' the moon changes phase.}}
##* '''2016''', [https://web.archive.org/web/20170925022505/https://learningenglish.voanews.com/a/lets-learn-english-lesson-4/3168920.html VOA Learning English] (public domain)
##*: '''Why''' do you have a map of the world?
##*:: {{audio|en|Why do you have a map of the world.ogg|Audio (US)}}
### {{non-gloss definition|With a negative, used rhetorically to make a suggestion.}}
###: '''''Why''' don't you ask her out for dinner?''
## {{non-gloss definition|Introducing a verb phrase (bare infinitive clause).}}
##: {{ux|en|'''Why''' spend money on something you already get for free?}}
##: {{ux|en|'''Why''' not tell him how you feel?}}
## {{non-gloss definition|Introducing a noun or other phrase.}}
##: {{ux|en|'''Why''' him? '''Why''' not someone taller?}}
# {{lb|en|relative}} For [[which]] [[cause]], [[reason]], or [[purpose]].
#: {{ux|en|That's the reason '''why''' I did that.}}
# {{lb|en|fused relative}} The [[cause]], [[reason]], or [[purpose]] for which.
#: ''That is '''why''' the sky is blue.''
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=2013-07-20|volume=408|issue=8845|magazine={{w|The Economist}}
|title=[http://www.economist.com/news/science-and-technology/21581981-what-pollution-some-opportunity-others-welcome-plastisphere Welcome to the plastisphere]
|passage=Plastics are energy-rich substances, which is '''why''' many of them burn so readily. Any organism that could unlock and use that energy would do well in the Anthropocene. Terrestrial bacteria and fungi which can manage this trick are already familiar to experts in the field.}}

